Z||000000||fropuff||07-25-2000||10:38 AM||||Hey.  I have a little problem.  When I was driving my '86 GT to the paint guys' house last week, I noticed that when I hit a bump in the crappy road, the odometer stops.  Might be common.  But, when I hit another one, the odometer starts to go BACKWARDS.  Not so common.  It's only on this road, though.  However, when I hit two more, (one to stop it and another to get it going forward) the odometer speeds up to make up for the lost numbers.  When it's back to normal, it runs fine until I get to that road.  I could take another way, but I have no license, insurance, title, or current plates yet.  I'm a sitting target for the old coppers.  This odometer problem doesn't bother me that much, but does anyone know if it can be fixed and if so, what does it need to be fixed?  Thanks.  ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||07-25-2000||11:17 AM||||<BR>Sounds like it may have been a temporal displacement.<P>Were you able to determine the effects of this area on your time pieces? Did they also stop, then start running backward in time, then stop, then work correctly?<P>It appears that this area my have some unseen energy flow.  What else occured while you were out there?<P>All kidding aside, how long has the car been sitting?  Maybe there is something in the speedsor sending the ecm the wrong message. It seems odd that this would happen, especially running backward.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||07-25-2000||11:23 AM||||i agree... deffinately sounds like a temperal displacement!<P>i would go back to the area in question, and scan it, with your tricorder, for any unseen anomilies... then, call the Paranoid Times for a full investigation, b4 the Suits get there to shut it down.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
