Z||000005||William Federle||07-25-2000||01:25 PM||||I just (hopefully) fixed the speedometer in my 1984 Fiero. It is run by a small stepper motor that has two wires connecting it to an electronics board behind the speedometer. The wires are connected with a plug. I had the thing apart 2 or three times, taping up a bare spot in the wire, and trying to get the odometer to read what I thought was the correct mileage (I wound it forward). Anyway after the 2nd try, it appeared to do what you said - a little bump seemed to make it go backward slightly. I took it apart again and soldered the wires to the terminals on the theory that the vibration from the bumps was causing a bad connection. It seems to have worked - it's been since Saturday - about 250 miles - and it still hasn't quit yet. I think the going backwards thing is some kind of mechanical thing. ||||reg||1
